  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Road Infrastructure Programme for Somalia (RIPSO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall Objective:Overall objective of the programme is to promote an enabling environment for higher economic growth and participation of the country in the Horn of Africa and the global economy.The Specific Objectives of the action:1.Is to improve management of the road sector at the national level, and in the states of Galmudug, Hirshabelle, Jubaland, and Puntland, and South West State of Somalia. 2.Is to improve transport connectivity for road users in targeted road corridors that will be rehabilitated in Galmudug, Hirshabelle, Jubaland, and Puntland regions of Somalia.Activities: 1.Technical Assistance and Capacity Building for Road Agencies in Somalia.2.Road Rehabilitations of:a)82 km rehabilitation and paving of the following sections of the existing 7.3m wide Belet Weyne-Galkayo paved road with surface dressing: Belet Weyne - Kalabeyr (22km) and Dhusamareb  Qaradhi (60km).b)85 km rehabilitation and paving of the following section of the existing 7.3m wide Galkayo-Garowe paved road with surface dressing: Galkayo  Faratoyoc)80 km gravelling and compacting of the Luuq, Ganane-Dolow existing 7.3m wide earth road</narrative>
  </description>
